From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:03:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): keep the sidebar's list filter, Select and bulk bar
 in view

The session filter, Select sessions and, while selecting, the
bulk-action bar sat in a section header inside the scrolling session
list: on the Sessions header with sidebar_grouping_ui off, on the
Projects header (or the first group's) with it on. Scrolling a long
list pushed them out of view, mid-selection included.

They now share one toolbar row above the scrolling list, in both
layouts. ConversationList portals it into a slot the sidebar renders
between its navigation and the list, so it keeps the list's state
without living inside the scroll container. Nothing scrolls under it,
so it needs no fill of its own and shows the sidebar's background in
every theme. The row is labelled with the current Display choice;
the Sessions header keeps New session and the Projects menu keeps
its own folder selection. The header slots that only carried these
controls are removed.

Carried here so the controls stay reachable on long lists before the
upstream PR lands.

Not upstream yet: proposed from fix/sidebar-sticky-session-toolbar; drop
this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
